      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-12-09_WidnesExaminer_art0098" n="art0098">
        <head>STOCKTON HEATH.</head>
        <p>STOCKTON HEATH.</p>
        <p>P.S.A.—The opening meeting of the Stockton Heath P.S.A. Society was held in the Wesleyan Church ors Sunday, and was fairly yell attended. Mr. %V. H.. Sherburn occupied the chair, and the Rev. J. Manning was the speaker, and h;s address proved very interest- ing and instructive. Miss Marie Houghton, of Dares. bury, rendr.red several solos in an effective ruauner.</p>
        <p>r..:ND OF BOPE MEETING.—A cinematograph enter- tainment was given on Monday evening in the new Wesleyan scnoolroom in connection with the Hill Cliffe and Stockton Heath United Band of Hope Society, a large attendance being presided over by the Rev. J. S. Hughes. The exhibition, which was of a very interest- ing iind amusing nature, was supplied by Mr. Clinton Lewis, of,Warrington. In addition to the numerous animated pictures a very pleasing variety of illustrated</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-12-09_WidnesExaminer_art0099" n="art0099">
        <head>PADGATE.</head>
        <p>PADGATE.</p>
        <p>DANCE AT THE KINGS CAFE.—The first dance and whist-drive, organized by the Padgate Cinderella Com- mittee took place on Friday evening at the Ring's Cafe. The uhist was under the direction of Mr. Percy Bennett. The ladies' first prize (a pretty sugar bowl and sifter) was won by Mrs. Liglatburn with a score of 181 points, while Mrs. Atkinson ,vou the second prize (a silver button hook) with a score of 178,peints. In the gentle- man's section the result was a tie of 166 points, a re- play being necessary. The ultimate winner was Mrs. Jennings (who was playing as a gentleman), Mr. P. Darbyshire being second. The claming was carried on to the strains of Mr. Pemberton's band, under the direction of Messrs. E, Atkinson and J. Percival, who acted as M.C.'s.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-12-09_WidnesExaminer_art0100" n="art0100">
        <head>BRONCHIAL ASTHMA. SUFFERED MANY YEARS. CURED BY VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE.</head>
        <p>BRONCHIAL ASTHMA. SUFFERED MANY YEARS. CURED BY VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE.</p>
        <p>Mrs. MARTIN HILL, The Hem, Shilnal, Salop, writes, March :31st, 1903 :—"I have had what the doctors I call bronchial asthma, and they said I should never be j cured, but thanks be to God and VKNG's LIGHTNING', CoUGII eRE lam better now than I have been for six years ; since I havs been taking your COUGH CURE I eau lie down and have a good night's. rest ; it seems a Godsend to me. I have recommended your COUGH CURE to several of my friends. During the winters I had to sit in a chair three months at a time because of shortness of breath and a choking sensation, but all that has gone and I am now looking very well." VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE is the safest and speediest remedy procurable for coughs, colds, bron- chitis, asthma, catarrh, pleurisy and children's coughs. ; Price 1);(1., Is. 11d. and s. 9d. at Chemists everywhere.</p>
