      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-12-09_WidnesExaminer_art0111" n="art0111">
        <head>RUNCORN Boy's THEFT,</head>
        <p>RUNCORN Boy's THEFT,</p>
        <p>At Runcorn on Monday, Thomas Winstanley, aged seventeen, of Runcorn, was charged with having stolen two watches, a watch guard, a spade ace guinea, and 55., the property of his father, Thomas Winstanley, a farmer. About eleven in the morning of the previous Monday the father went out to work, leaving the prisoner in the house. When he returned he found that the youth had gone, and the articles mentioned above were missing. They had been taken out of his deceased wife's trunk. It was found that he had gone to Altrincham and joined a theatrical company. The father did riot wish to press the case, and on the accused promising to be better in the future he was discharged.</p>
